{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkYTM5qPg5D9ZSrcX1sv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0169HBtUNtNKoP8JDWDn3hxZ","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"working":"The line opens with an F clef and two flats. Bar 1 of the line is edition bar 86. It has paired 8ths: D4 and C4 above the staff with ledger lines, each followed by F3 on the fourth line, giving D4 F3 D4 F3 C4 F3 C4 F3. Bar 2 is bar 87: Bb3 F3 Bb3 F3 A3 F3 A3 F3, with the upper notes now inside the staff. Bar 3 is bar 88, four quarters: Bb3, then a flat on Ab3, a flat on Gb3, and F3. Bar 4 is bar 89: a natural sign before an E3 (a half note in the edition), an F3 quarter, then a quarter rest. Bar 5 is bar 90. It repeats bar 86's pattern, D4 F3 D4 F3 C4 F3 C4 F3, and closes with the final barline at the right edge. No dynamics or slurs can be read. That does not affect the match.","right":true,"insights":"Bars 86–89 repeat as 90–93, so the line's first bar alone can't fix where it starts. The written accidentals help: the flats on Ab and Gb in bar 88 and the natural on E in bar 89. So does the line ending on an 8th-note bar right after bar 89. Ruling out a start at bar 90 means seeing that the line's last bar is 8ths, not quarters (bar 92) or half notes (bar 93), or knowing where the line before ends."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5365,"cache_read_input_tokens":523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5365},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0e0f773-fad0-420c-9d74-56d63c79b27f","uuid":"67961754-aae9-40a6-9b17-fcf871440c29","timestamp":"2026-11-05T22:08:05.185Z","request_id":"req_011CgkYTLkVcUb67